./logs/iter_001_idea_01_explorer_02_critic_02.stderr.log:1073:iterations/iter_001/idea_01/explorer_01.md:3:The sparse vanishing-spike refutation checks out under the literal per-process reading of the conjecture. It gives a process with \(\beta(h)=1\) for every \(h\), yet the learner that always posts \(0\) has regret at most \(1\) for every horizon. So the stated “only if” direction is false as written.
./logs/iter_001_idea_01_explorer_02_critic_02.stderr.log:1074:iterations/iter_001/idea_01/explorer_01.md:5:The core flaw exposed is that \(\beta\) is an unweighted delay-tail condition: it counts long delays for quotes whose payoff scale is negligible, especially \(a=0\).
