./logs/iter_001_idea_01_explorer_02_critic_02.stderr.log:1107:iterations/iter_001/idea_01/explorer_02.md:3:The sparse vanishing-spike refutation is valid under the literal per-process reading of the conjecture. The failure is quantifier-level: \(\beta\) takes a worst-case supremum over actions, times, and histories, and therefore counts long delays for \(a=0\), even though those delays carry zero payoff and need not create regret.
