./logs/iter_001_idea_03_explorer_01.stderr.log:855:A self-contained finite-delay proof can avoid invoking a heavy delayed-feedback theorem. Split times into residue classes modulo \(H+1\). On one residue class, by the next occurrence of that residue, all \(H\)-truncated reward vectors from the previous occurrence have matured. Run an independent full-information Hedge instance on each residue class.
