./logs/iter_001_idea_03_explorer_02.stdout.log:5:The obstruction is not technical: large long-horizon tail reward can be perfectly predictable or distributionally known, so the learner may not need delayed reward feedback to choose the right quote. I found a concrete counterexample where `Delta_T(H_T)` is linear along infinitely many horizons for every `H_T log T = o(T)`, while a fixed learner has `o(T)` regret.
./logs/iter_001_idea_03_explorer_02.stdout.log:9:The proposed replacement tail quantity is
