./logs/iter_001_idea_01_explorer_01_critic_01.stderr.log:1052:./iterations/iter_001/idea_01/explorer_02.md:120:Replace unweighted \(\beta\) by a payoff-weighted or horizon-level condition. The sparse-spike example has \(\beta\equiv1\) but satisfies the heuristic bound \(a\Pr[h<\tau_t(a)<\infty]\lesssim 1/h\), which is why it is easy despite maximal unweighted tail failure.
